    "body": "## Summary\n- preflight a publication through the existing locked publication read before creating its Stripe PaymentIntent\n- commit expiry settlement and idempotent `JOB_PUBLICATION_RELEASE` before returning a terminal conflict for stale publications\n- keep the actual Stripe intent service as the second, independently revalidated step\n- add regression coverage proving an expired reserve is released, private payload is cleared, and Stripe is never called\n\n## Why\nThe payment-intent endpoint intentionally avoided mutating an expired publication in the same transaction that throws `409`, because that mutation would be rolled back. The side effect was that a stale wallet reservation could remain until scheduler/recovery. Splitting the preflight into its own service transaction lets the existing expiry path commit safely before the coordinator rejects intent creation.\n\n## Validation\nLatest-head CI must be fully green before merge. No Flyway migration is required.",
